    "type": "question",
    "label": "50",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$2^{2x+2}+2^{x+2}-3=0.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-1$.\n\nLet $u=2^x>0$ and reject the negative root of the quadratic in $u$.",
      "worked": "Let $u=2^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4u^2+4u-3&=0\\\\(2u-1)(2u+3)&=0\\\\u&=\\frac12\\text{ or }u=-\\frac32.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $u=-\\frac32$ because $2^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x&=\\frac12\\\\2^x&=2^{-1}\\\\x&=-1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
